 "trap": "false_fail",
 "expected": "pass",
 "why": "Done but odd: same step (Intro to CAD lesson 5). The learner left the Pocket's Type at Dimension with FreeCAD's default Length of 5 mm instead of switching to Through all. The plate is exactly 5 mm thick, so the pocket ends on the bottom face: both 4 mm holes, at X 10 and X 50, go all the way through (the shape's holes are through, volume 11874.3 = 12000 minus two 4 mm cylinders). Through all would only matter if the plate later got thicker; the step's outcome holds now.",
 "step": {
  "id": "s5",
  "index": 5,
  "title": "Sketch on a face and cut holes",
  "file": "plate.FCStd",
  "instructions": "Select the top face of the plate and click Create sketch. Draw two circles 10 mm in from each short end on the centre line (centres at X 10 and X 50, Y 20) and give each a 4 mm Diameter constraint. Close the sketch, click Pocket and set Type to Through all. Save (Cmd+S).",
